Good work, everyone!

35
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:25,660
I was so nervous up there.

36
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:26,460
My knees were shaking!

37
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:30,180
You were both really fantastic!

38
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,820
You were so cool!

39
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:32,860
Yeah, you were!

40
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:33,940
That's my sister!

41
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:35,520
Mm-hmm.

42
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,880
Chieri, you were amazing, too!

43
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,220
Really?

44
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:43,160
Memori-san, you were overflowing with pheromones!

45
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,840
Oh, really?

46
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,200
Do you think so?

47
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,960
You did great, Megu.

48
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:48,240
Ugh.

49
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,440
Oh, Megu?

50
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,640
What are you doing?

51
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:59,480
I found a video of the members participating in the peace ceremony on the news.

52
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,120
What?

53
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:02,040
What?

54
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:02,600
Let's see!

55
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,200
What is that?

56
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:09,520
World of Justice 0048 gave the citizens courage with their beautiful voices.

57
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,520
Oh!

58
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,900
Oh, man.

59
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:15,300
It disappeared.

60
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,880
DES interference.

61
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:20,240
But Takamina-san was so cool.

62
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,760
Kanata, you're a total Takamina-san supporter.

63
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:25,940
It's not like that, really.

64
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,100
Kanata-san.

65
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:28,640
What?

66
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,880
Takamina-san and the others should be coming home now.

67
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:32,400
Huh?

68
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:34,860
Oh, no!

69
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:34,920
Oh, no!

70
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,280
Sister.

71
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,780
She sure loves Takamina-san, doesn't she?

72
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:46,420
Yeah.

73
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,200
Let's go welcome them home, too.

74
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:49,080
Yeah, I guess so.

75
00:04:49,080 --> 00:05:01,340
Takamina-san!

76
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,020
Huh?

77
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:04,400
Good work today!

78
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:05,440
Thanks.

79
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:09,080
I hope you put on a good performance in our absence.

80
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:10,080
Did you?

81
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:10,940
Yeah!

82
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:12,620
Now you've said it.

83
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,720
I'll check the video later to see how you did.

84
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,580
Ow.

85
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:19,380
You guys didn't like it, guys!

86
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,760
Let's get this meeting started.

87
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:26,160
The planet of our next concert, Tundra Star,

88
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:29,140
is under the effect of a total entertainment ban.

89
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,940
The fans there demand an appearance from us,

90
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:34,140
but we cannot avoid conflict with the DES.

91
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,300
It will be an unpredictable guerrilla concert.

92
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:38,400
Guerrilla concert?

93
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:40,860
A planet with a total entertainment ban?

94
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,340
Conflict is unavoidable.

95
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:46,620
Consequently, we will be taking special measures for this concert.

96
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:47,300
Kanata.

97
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:47,860
Yes!

98
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:48,500
Memori.

99
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:49,340
Yes!

100
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:49,880
Megumi.

101
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,000
Yes!

102
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:56,500
And finally, all the 77th Generation trainees.

103
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,120
You'll be understudies.

104
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,700
You want understudies to perform at a guerrilla concert?

105
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:02,480
Amazing.

106
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:07,400
I can't believe we'll have the chance to appear on stage!

107
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,600
Hold on a minute.

108
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:10,700
Why the 77th Generation?

109
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:13,560
Why am I the only one from the 76th Generation?

110
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:18,880
Can the 76th Generation sing and dance all the songs on today's set list?

111
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:19,920
Well, answer me.

112
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,540
Despite not being selected as members,

113
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:26,740
the entire 77th Generation continued to practice.

114
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:30,500
What was the 76th Generation doing during that time?

115
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,400
I told you before,

116
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,920
the only thing to do is practice.

117
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,040
That's all.

118
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:47,560
Takamina-san!

119
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:47,860
Huh?

120
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,400
Do you have a minute?

121
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:52,960
It's Kanata.

122
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,280
I'm so glad I caught you.

123
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:58,920
You can count on me being your understudy.

124
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,220
I'll do my very best.

125
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:01,740
You don't need to worry about a thing.

126
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,520
I won't let you down.

127
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,640
Yeah, thanks.

128
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,700
You just keep practicing.

129
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:07,480
Yeah!

130
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,520
Kanata!

131
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:09,900
Huh?

132
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:12,880
Everyone's already heading towards the station!

133
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:13,740
Okay!

134
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,500
Well, good luck on your next job then.

135
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:20,860
Takamina.

136
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,600
Huh?

137
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:25,240
Do you think I did something wrong?

138
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:27,060
Huh?

139
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:31,940
How do you think the original Takamina-san

140
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:34,480
would have reacted in that kind of situation?

141
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:37,760
I'm sure that

142
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:41,120
she would have smiled and motivated her junior.

143
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:45,560
I don't really understand anymore.

144
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:48,740
I couldn't make a very Takamina-like expression.

145
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,940
I don't know what's come over me.

146
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,600
I don't know what's going over me.

147
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,600
I don't know what's going over me.

148
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:58,260
This is so frustrating!

149
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:00,080
Please don't cry, Hazuki.

150
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:02,920
But we became trainees way before them!

151
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,200
It's just not fair!

152
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:07,000
Come on, calm down.

153
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,020
Kanata-san.

154
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:11,480
Please, there's no need to get so worked up.

155
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:13,780
Girls who work hard will get their turn eventually.

156
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,720
Let's grab the next chance when it comes.

157
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,560
You've got a point.

158
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:21,160
Next time.

159
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:25,360
Is that really what you believe?

160
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,820
What about you, Kanata-senpai?

161
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:28,940
What do you believe?

162
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,400
Your opportunity has never come,

163
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:34,220
but you still keep working hard as a trainee.

164
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:35,600
If it were me,

165
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:38,040
I'd be too ashamed to continue in Zero Zero.

166
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:41,880
What did you say?

167
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,820
Sonata, it's okay.

168
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,000
That's unforgivable!

169
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,560
Starting to date, I'll call you nasty!

170
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,560
Take this!

171
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,460
Sonata!

172
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:54,720
Sonata, I headbutted you.

173
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:58,520
If I headbutt you, it hurts me just as much.

174
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,540
So I won't apologize.

175
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,300
But Megumi-san,

176
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:04,800
I demand that you apologize to Kanata-san!

177
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:07,840
Megu, let's go!

178
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:08,980
I'm sorry.

179
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:10,260
I'm really sorry.

180
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:10,360
I'm sorry.

181
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,280
Megumi-san has a head like a rock.

182
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,400
You've got a bomb!

183
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:25,360
Pain, pain, go away to Megumi!

184
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,160
Suzuko, thanks.

185
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:28,960
Kanata-san.

186
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,520
But it's okay.

187
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,960
I actually understand how they feel.

188
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:35,700
We were pretty upset too, you know?

189
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:36,340
Yeah.

190
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:38,800
Kanata's right.

191
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:44,580
When Yoko, I mean, when Sei became a successor before us, we panicked.

192
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:45,940
It was terrible.

193
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:49,040
Sai-san was part of the 76th generation?

194
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:50,360
That's right.

195
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,360
But she's so nice.

196
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,760
She felt sorry for us.

197
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,660
She was so apologetic.

198
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,500
All of us felt really bad about it.

199
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:00,200
Yeah.

200
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,080
Come on.

201
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,140
Chef Papa's dinner is waiting for us.

202
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,600
Let's go back to the dorm.

203
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:07,360
Okay!

204
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:11,320
I'm really sorry for your soul and the idea of a house.

205
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,320
Oh, that's great.

206
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:28,960
An understudy at a concert.

207
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:31,940
I wonder if someone like me can do it.

208
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,140
You shouldn't sell yourself short.

209
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:34,740
Huh?

210
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,000
If you don't perform with confidence,

211
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,980
it's rude to the girls who weren't chosen to be on stage.

212
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:44,120
I've always thought you were kind of nice, T-Eddie.

213
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,920
That's really good advice, you know?

214
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:46,720
What?

215
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,160
You're right.

216
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,340
I'll try to be confident.

217
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:56,060
Hey, when you get nervous, do your molars ever itch?

218
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:56,800
Hmm?

219
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,440
Ah, right here!

220
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,060
See?

221
00:10:59,060 --> 00:10:59,820
What was that for, T-Eddie?

222
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:13,400
I thought you might be able to fit an entire orange in your huge mouth.

223
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,520
Oh, that's impossible.

224
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,520
Oh, cheery.

225
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,520
How are you doing?

226
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,640
I will be performing in a concert as an understudy soon.

227
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:24,640
I'm moving closer to my dream of becoming one of the idols that you hate, but...

228
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:29,640
But someday, Mamoru, I hope you'll come see me perform on stage.

229
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,760
So, uh...

230
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,760
You guys shouldn't snoop like that.

231
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,760
It's not nice.

232
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:33,760
It's a letter.

233
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,760
And it's addressed to a boy.

234
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:54,640
First, we'll enter the target sector with Kaiusha and get a read on the situation.

235
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:58,300
Then, we'll descend a Tundra Star in the Flying Ghet.

236
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,560
Let us go to meet our adoring fans.

237
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:14,880
We haven't slept in these beds for a while, huh?

238
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:19,880
Hey, I look forward to working with you, Megumi-san.

239
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:22,380
So, shall we go practice?

240
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,380
What?

241
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,880
But I thought we just finished practicing!

242
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,380
No excuses.

243
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,140
Katsuyusha's got a lesson room we can use now.

244
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,880
Let's get to work, guys!

245
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:34,380
Wow, Kaneda-san's sure fired up, isn't she?

246
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:39,000
Haha, I'm sure she doesn't want to let down her beloved Takamina-san!

247
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,500
Did you say something?

248
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,500
Hehehehe!

249
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,500
Oh!

250
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,500
Oh, come on and practice with us.

251
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,500
No thanks.

252
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:46,500
I'll pass.

253
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,500
Megumi…

254
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:50,500
Bye-bye, Nasty!

255
00:12:50,500 --> 00:13:02,620
I love you, I am in love with you, I will run with all the strength I have.

256
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:06,120
Why are you practicing with Kaneda-san and the others?

257
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,120
Yoko.

258
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,120
It's Se now.

259
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,620
I'm not Yoko anymore.

260
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:13,620
You'll always be Yoko!

261
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:15,240
What's wrong, Megu?

262
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,240
You're acting really strange.

263
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,740
You think I'm acting strange?

264
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:21,240
There's no way you could understand me anymore, Yoko!

265
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,240
Uh…

266
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:28,240
You left everyone else in the 76th generation behind and became a successor.

267
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:32,240
We used to be together all the time, but now we're always apart.

268
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,240
Megu…

269
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,240
I'm sorry.

270
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,240
What are you apologizing for?

271
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,240
Uh…

272
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:37,240
I guess you're right.

273
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:52,240
It'd be better if you didn't try to associate with trainees.

274
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,240
Seisan.

275
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,240
Megu…

276
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,240
Whoa!

277
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:58,240
That's crazy!

278
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:03,240
Rene, aren't you on a diet?

279
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:07,240
Thanks to our hard lessons, I lost a little weight, so I quit.

280
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,240
Whoa!

